From 35d495f368bd49089b8f4741b1d839603a2e6e2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nura <nura@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:50:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] panfrost/kmod: add a kbase (UK 10.6) backend

The Nura 3.10 kernel exposes ARM kbase r15p0 through /dev/mali0 instead of
DRM: per-fd contexts, SAME_VA memory mapped at BO allocation time, 64-byte
base_jd_atom_v2 submissions and Android-sync-fence soft jobs.

Add pan_kmod_kbase, implementing device discovery/handshake, GPU props,
BO allocation/mmap/free, a no-op VM (kbase installs mappings at mmap),
submission with in/out fences, a binary sync provider on kbase fences and
JM context stubs.  The pan_kmod ops table gains optional submit_job and
jm_ctx_create/jm_ctx_destroy hooks so the DRM path is unchanged.

Includes a standalone kbase-kmod test that validates fd rejection without
hardware.
